{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>From the end</b> — He mentioned its circuits according to its true generation, which is opposite the great circuit." "And the word תקופה is like \"for the days of the feast <i>had made a circuit</i>\" (Esther 1:4), \"they <i>surrounded</i> me.\"" "And the sense of <b>and nothing is hidden</b> — for the heat of the sun in the world is like the likeness of the heart's heat in the body of man, a proof of the wisdom of generation; and behold, it is the life of all bodies."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:49.269827949Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}